Separate note on the instance-workspace feature (MIT, no derived code)

The instance-management feature (per-instance launch overrides, loader install,
mod / resource-pack / shader / world management) studies the *feature
decomposition and data organisation* of HMCL (https://github.com/HMCL-dev/HMCL),
which is distributed under GPL-3.0. That licence is not compatible with this
MIT-licensed crate, so no Java source, constant table, UI string, class name or
asset is copied or translated.

What was studied: which settings may be overridden per instance, how a version
directory is laid out, how mod metadata files are prioritised, how the resource
pack list is stored in `options.txt`, and which fields of `level.dat` a launcher
shows.

What was written for TMCL: every module under `src/core/content/`,
`src/core/instance/overrides.rs`, `src/tui/pages/workspace.rs`,
`src/tui/app/workspace*.rs` and `src/tui/app/preset/workspace.rs`, including the
scanner, metadata parsers, trash/backup logic and all rendering.

HMCL is not a dependency, not a vendored subtree and not a source of copied
code; it is a behavioural reference only.

## nightlight preset (nightlightd)

The `nightlight` TUI preset studies the *visual language* of `nightlightd`
(https://github.com/umdinceryananer/nightlightd), version 0.3.1, which is
distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later. That licence is not compatible with this
MIT-licensed crate, so no Rust source, constant table, function body, string or
ASCII layout is copied or translated.

What was studied: one accent colour deriving a whole brightness ladder, the
absence of card borders, a numbered icon sidebar whose selected row is a
full-width accent bar, a single full-width footer under the sidebar, and a
"live" accent that warms with the clock.

What was written for TMCL: every module under `src/tui/nightlight/` and
`src/tui/app/nightlight/`, plus `src/tui/modal/render_nightlight.rs`. The palette
ratios, the black-body curve, the smoothstep clock ramps and the layout were
re-derived and are asserted value-by-value in-tree
(`src/tui/nightlight/tone.rs`, `live.rs`). Colour values were chosen by hue from
the public screenshots, not read out of the reference source.

`nightlightd` is not a dependency, not a vendored subtree and not a source of
copied code; it is a design reference only.

## shelf preset (tuiba)

The `shelf` TUI preset studies the *visual language* of `tuiba`
(https://github.com/Huseynteymurzade28/tuiba), revision
e4cab2c32d0336d069993b5c6ba8d259da97ba1b, which is distributed under the MIT
License.

What was studied: one accent colour over a neutral ink ladder, a rounded panel
outline that leaves the page colour showing through, a selection that fades out
towards the right instead of filling the whole row, and a side-by-side
list/preview split with a persistent facts column.

What was written for TMCL: every module under `src/tui/app/view/shelf/`, plus
`src/tui/modal/shelf.rs`, `src/tui/widgets/cover.rs` and `src/core/cover.rs`.
The palette was re-derived and is asserted for contrast in-tree
(`src/tui/app/view/shelf/tone.rs`); the secondary ink was raised from tuiba's
`#6F6888` (3.59:1 on the page) to `#8A82A8` (5.23:1) to meet this project's
4.5:1 floor. The half-block cover pipeline, the cover source order
(`icon.png` → newest world screenshot → procedural tile) and the placeholder
pattern are original to TMCL.

tuiba is not a dependency, not a vendored subtree and not a source of copied
code; it is a design reference only. Unlike the GPL references above, its MIT
licence would have allowed copying — the preset is nevertheless an independent
implementation, because a colour table means nothing without this project's
semantic tokens.
